I checked the Q4 half kernel against `q27_matmul_q4_mm` and `q27_matmul_t2_mm_h`. The Q4-specific substitutions look consistent: packed weight row stride uses `cols / 2`, weight scale row stride and flush index use `cols / 64`, the final activation scale index stays within `cols / 32`, and the LUT decodes bytes low-nibble first to match the float kernel’s LSB-first unpack.

The row and token clamping pattern matches the mature half T2 path: out-of-range row loads clamp and stores are guarded; out-of-range token lanes read the last valid token/scales but never store. The barrier structure also matches the T2 half schedule: per-simdgroup scratch only needs simdgroup barriers, and the final threadgroup barrier protects `Wt`/`Xt` before the next tile staging.

No dangling Q8 route showed up. `q27_matmul_q8_mm_h` is present only as a parked kernel/comment reference; backend dispatch still routes `Q8_G128` to `q27_matmul_q8_mm`.

